{"Race condition in blocked email counter: Multiple concurrent signups hitting the same blocked email will each read the current match_count, add 1, and save. Because this is a read-modify-write sequence without any locking, later saves can clobber earlier increments and the statistics (including last_match_at) become inaccurate. Should use atomic database update instead.": 0.8744880557060242, "emailValidation computed property depends on 'rejectedEmails.@each', but @each only reacts to property changes on array items, not to items being added/removed. After the server rejects an email and pushes it into rejectedEmails, the computed property doesn't recompute, so the UI still shows the email as valid. Should use 'rejectedEmails.[]' instead to track collection changes.": 0.8674784898757935}